    "incident_title": "Payments retry storm knocked over fraud-svc?",
    "outcome": "conclusive",
    "summary": "The reporter's hypothesis (payments retries overloaded fraud-svc and caused the crash) is not supported as the root cause. The evidence points to fraud-svc being OOM-killed at 10:02:08, about 1 second before payments-svc logged its first fraud-check failure. The likely trigger is the scheduled fraud-gbm v6 to v7 model hot-reload at 09:30, which roughly doubled the model footprint (0.8GB to 1.9GB serialized) against a 2048Mi container limit. Container memory climbed steadily from about 1.16GB at 09:30 to about 2.01GB at 10:00 while request rate stayed flat near 310 rps. Retries are real and visible, but they appear only after the restart (the 1.7x inbound surge is logged at 10:05:30), so they amplified the outage rather than starting it. Retries are already capped at 3 attempts per the logs. Retry limits alone would not have prevented this OOM; the memory budget for the v7 model is the primary fix.",
    "root_cause": "fraud-svc was OOM-killed (exit 137, container limit 2048Mi) during/after the scheduled fraud-gbm v6->v7 model hot-reload at 09:30. The v7 model (1.9GB serialized, 340 added features) pushed the working set from about 1.16GB toward the 2GiB limit; the pod was killed at 10:02:08. payments-svc connection resets began at 10:02:09. Client retries and the post-restart traffic surge then amplified the impact. The mechanism (v7 in-memory footprint causing the growth) is inferred from timing and has not been confirmed with a heap profile.",
